          "parts": [
            "We are given the equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + A = \\frac{B}{C}\n\\]\n\nWith values:\n\n- \\( A = 10.957 \\)\n- \\( C = 0.510998950 \\)\n\n### Step 1: Plug in the values\n\\[\n1 + 10.957 = \\frac{B}{0.510998950}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n11.957 = \\frac{B}{0.510998950}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Solve for \\( B \\)\n\\[\nB = 11.957 \\times 0.510998950\n\\]\n\n\\[\nB \\approx 6.105295\n\\]\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\\[\nB \\approx 6.1053\n\\]\n\nWould you like this answer with more decimal places or in scientific notation?"
